Assistant: At what point in the voyage or reporting cycle should the logbook data be submitted electronically—for example, after each catch event, before arrival in port, at landing/transhipment, or only after the master or owner has completed a final review—and are there any deadlines or triggers that govern submission timing?
User: My understanding is that the system needs to support ongoing recording during the voyage, but submission timing will depend on the type of report and the regulatory trigger. In practice, some entries may need to be sent at landing or transhipment, while the full logbook may be finalised after the master has reviewed it and then submitted within whatever deadline the fisheries administration requires.
I don’t know the exact deadlines offhand, and I’d want to check the rules for each administration because those timings can differ. What matters most operationally is that the system clearly prompts the user when a submission is due and doesn’t let them miss a required reporting point.
